piper_tabletop_sim
==================

This package contains code, URDF/xacro, Gazebo world files and meshes derived
from the following sources. The original copyright and license notices remain
in effect for the derived portions.

1. AgileX PiPER arm and gripper
   - Official model: agx_arm_urdf/piper (AgileX Robotics).
   - Link masses, inertias, joint origins and limits, and gripper finger meshes
     are the official PiPER values.
   - The arm macro and mesh set were also transcribed in
     ag_robot_description (MIT), which was used as the local reference.

2. ag_robot_description
   - Source project: ag_robot_description.
   - License: MIT.
   - Used for: PiPER arm macro structure, D435i body pose and intrinsics,
     camera/optical frame layout, Gazebo sensor and ros2_control patterns.
   - The camera pitch override (default 60 deg down) is a tabletop-demo
     addition, not part of the original vehicle model.

3. piper_lightweight_sim
   - Source project: piper_lightweight_sim.
   - License: Apache-2.0.
   - Used as the Gazebo Harmonic scene/launch skeleton, table layout and
     single-arm + D435i composition.

4. Intel RealSense D435i
   - The D435i mesh and reference intrinsics are from the librealsense /
     RealSense reference device data, as transcribed in ag_robot_description.

